n really really compliant  it's really good news that people want  to do their uh part to make sure that we  get this virus under control and yes the  prime minister said that you know plan b  is working there'll be a cabinet meeting  today and i i don't see any reason why  we need to change it's important that we  do follow the data we've done that all  along and we'll continue to do that and  you know people are playing their part  and i want to thank them for that  you talking about the vaccines and how  important they are um  why are we then selling off at a uk  vaccine development center near oxford  the the vaccine manufacturing and  innovation center i mean that doesn't  seem like a  great confidence boost does it that if  we are selling off these facilities as  soon as they appear successful  well i wouldn't want to comment on the  commercial decision but i think what is  important that we've got um good supply  of vaccines you know we've we've got the  the fires in the modern astrazeneca and  others coming online as well and it's  important that people do come forward uh  for those first vaccines and the second  one as well  that offer is always open and i think  what was really encouraging as well as  the booster program uh was turbocharged  more people came forward for their first  dose as well i think they've seen just  how important it is they've seen other  people get the vaccine and they've also  sadly heard the people say that they've  been seriously ill because they haven't  well they haven't had the vaccine and to  put that message out that vaccines are  important that do as save people from  getting serious disease and they do save  lives  yeah despite that we still have six  trusts and critical incidents um maggie  through parliamentary under secretary of  state for vaccines and public health  thank you very much

